def runRounds(
    members, world, d, turns:NoneType=None, Ttot:NoneType=None, t0:float=0.0, threads:int=8
):
Rounds of window d. A round starts at the earliest pending start s and takes every member whose next event starts in [s, s + d) (with d = 0, only the earliest one, ties to the lower index: the event-driven loop). Their events are prepared one after another in agent order at s, decided concurrently, and applied in (start, index) order; an event a member starts later inside the same window is prepared and decided when its turn comes, in event order. Each member stops after turns events (int or list) or once its next start reaches t0 + Ttot.
