RuleBridge
def RuleBridge(
    channel, rng, share:str='needed', guess:float=0.0
):
Mixin for an honest numpy member on a bridge board (bridgeMembers builds Bridge&lt;class&gt; from its class, so knownFor and everything else stay the base agent’s: a ColonyAgent on colony arms, flag-aware on failFlag boards). Roles are read at act time. A bridge (board.bridgeOf) first relays the leading mirror value (most senders, then earliest) of an open coupled subtask of its pair with no value of the cross clue on its board; otherwise it acts as its base agent. Every member, at its sharing step, first posts a held cross clue on its mirror when the mirror’s leading value is missing, different or unconfirmed (ColonyAgent’s rule, P22-12). A mirror share is applied to the board only, never posted to the channel.




