    valueOnly:bool=False, tokenClip:bool=False, klClamp:NoneType=None
):
epochs passes over samples (micro-batches chunks; passes after the first in a seeded shuffled order); the reference (adapter off) and old log-probabilities once, before the first pass; per pass: the clipped term plus kl x k3 to the reference, gradient clipping 1.0, one optimizer step. -&gt; loss, KL, tokens (the last pass’s). Pilot v3’s fix: valueOnly weights the loss and KL by valueMask (and adds klAll, the KL over every token); tokenClip clips each token’s ratio (tokenTerm) instead of the reply-level mean. Phase 18 Part B: klClamp caps each token’s k3 (loss and logged KL), so one token the policy scores far below the reference cannot dominate either.




